WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.775
Next you plan against a fictional
tenant without sending anything.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:07.772
The plan explains itself: the
context and strength get created,

3
00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:12.461
two objects get small updates, one
matches, and three policies are blocked,

4
00:00:12.461 --> 00:00:16.150
because the strength and context
they need don't exist yet.

5
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.300
A portal-made policy is
reported, never deleted.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.875
Then you apply to the fake three times.

7
00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:26.222
The first run creates the building
blocks, the second creates the three

8
00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:30.200
blocked policies in report-only,
and the third finds nothing to do.

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.050
That's what a safe,
repeatable write looks like.
